{"h":3209,"w":2400,"lines":[{"y":0.040419871772036875,"t":"Sample Writing answers","h":0.020568607603649536,"c":1,"x":0.085112092035379255,"w":0.23168884277343751},{"h":0.024922118380062308,"t":"TEST 1, WRITING TASK 2","x":0.08737864009259852,"y":0.090031152528475489,"c":1,"w":0.35922330220540366},{"c":1,"h":0.020946476541204184,"w":0.8117931620279949,"t":"This model has been prepared by an examiner as an example of a very good answer.","x":0.087283490636417493,"y":0.12708968789867692},{"y":0.1550160860262213,"w":0.81972920735677079,"t":"Scientific developments are occurring at a great rate but some of them do not seem to be of help","x":0.087224016732767307,"c":1,"h":0.025954339808764049},{"c":1,"y":0.17711647789868179,"t":"to people. In fact, sometimes scientific innovations are regretted by those who invented them. This","x":0.085300061213680459,"w":0.81779362996419269,"h":0.024906314124942153},{"h":0.024592636678820501,"y":0.19852386055954518,"c":1,"t":"essay will argue that science should never harm people but scientists should aim to further their","x":0.087211448250596679,"w":0.81585271199544263},{"t":"understanding as much as to improve people's lives.","x":0.087175519428606574,"h":0.023708086815949825,"y":0.22183998336175259,"c":1,"w":0.44109319051106766},{"y":0.24972240156590764,"w":0.77313023885091137,"x":0.08723069992570838,"c":1,"h":0.0254286828442154,"t":"On one hand, there is a strong argument that the public good should be the top priority for"},{"h":0.022547644023954705,"c":1,"y":0.27248025556708999,"w":0.82544565836588546,"t":"scientists. They are the ones who have the potential to make discoveries and invent things that can","x":0.087274393414291662},{"w":0.82746566772460928,"h":0.024698075624269844,"t":"change the worla. Electricity, modern medicine, telecommunications and the internet are just some","c":1,"x":0.087251041341249905,"y":0.29348818567772272},{"t":"of the scientific innovations that have changed lives for the better.","h":0.023350444092557376,"c":1,"y":0.31587430708647912,"x":0.087242349907552169,"w":0.55752166748046872},{"y":0.34515603745413626,"w":0.82540293375651042,"t":"On the other hand, sometimes scientists do research just in the hope of adding to their knowledge.","x":0.089229578453496092,"c":1,"h":0.022589131530571516},{"c":1,"y":0.36602084632233534,"x":0.087277738371237673,"t":"While they should make absolutely sure that their experiments do no harm, they may not know until","w":0.83716023763020841,"h":0.024547093233958206},{"h":0.023638743700639564,"y":0.38760902400931041,"x":0.087274325434803943,"t":"they have finished how their findings will be used and whether they will improve people's lives. The","c":1,"w":0.82351689656575533},{"t":"scientist Nobel invented dynamite to help with mining, not knowing that it would one day be used in","w":0.83525248209635417,"h":0.024978889631705137,"y":0.40920318313564863,"c":1,"x":0.089171645088334417},{"h":0.022458579755646468,"c":1,"w":0.80593694051106768,"t":"weapons, and the scientist who discovered the life-saving drug penicillin did so quite by chance.","x":0.089251395194674316,"y":0.43121260290818819},{"t":"Overall, it seems that science should improve the lives of people and that ought to be one of its","x":0.089172736537243794,"w":0.80031743367513031,"h":0.025112650030498562,"c":1,"y":0.46008250288260111},{"y":0.48188939053489555,"w":0.78476826985677095,"c":1,"t":"aims. However, knowledge and discovery are aims in themselves and are just as important for","x":0.089177266635114827,"h":0.024650894592855632},{"h":0.024095474670980499,"y":0.50370937667031901,"w":0.80610580444335944,"c":1,"t":"scientists. Sometimes scientists do not know how their scientific breakthroughs will be used until","x":0.089184404671048198},{"w":0.16000134785970055,"c":1,"x":0.088969715571687966,"y":0.52734316793014413,"t":"their work is done.","h":0.019305532817899929},{"c":1,"y":0.56523364544216859,"x":0.091164764446623303,"h":0.017709160445263827,"t":"Here are comments from another examiner:","w":0.41567990620930989},{"h":0.020995485299844296,"c":1,"x":0.13776307790722664,"w":0.77109156290690106,"t":"This response presents a well-developed response to the question and concludes","y":0.60088162725234728},{"w":0.77669901529947927,"x":0.13592234249589125,"y":0.61918604655180332,"c":1,"h":0.018895348284474811,"t":"that the aim of scientific discoveries should be to improve people's lives, but that"},{"c":1,"h":0.018777264984225939,"w":0.47974934895833338,"t":"the process often results in unexpected outcomes.","x":0.13584608608233334,"y":0.63981655704045937},{"c":1,"t":"hat exdid teastion, withb caddsate the skalaiming t Th ths axtent cale it iways","w":0.76111109415690104,"y":0.67499999997321436,"x":0.15555556348900987,"h":0.037499999999999978},{"t":"be predicted.","x":0.13786407768979606,"h":0.016199376947040434,"c":1,"y":0.71651090353783298,"w":0.12815533955891925},{"y":0.74949980272411099,"x":0.13778692427324196,"w":0.76521514892578146,"c":1,"h":0.020423012136298935,"t":"The candidate presents the argument that the true aim of science is gaining new"},{"w":0.74784810384114575,"h":0.023538162849402466,"c":1,"t":"knowledge and discoveries. They agree that this should be to improve people's","y":0.76731910974244089,"x":0.13773488513707405},{"y":0.78909657339092032,"c":1,"w":0.40970873514811201,"x":0.13786407910856402,"h":0.016199376947040545,"t":"lives but that the results can't be predicted."},{"w":0.68571136474609373,"t":"The second paragraph gives examples of discoveries that have changed","x":0.13967879218223128,"y":0.82372068007163413,"c":1,"h":0.0217247508396613},{"h":0.020381439066378904,"c":1,"t":"people's lives for the better [Electricity, modern medicine, telecommunications and","x":0.13980582432135019,"y":0.84299065447510024,"w":0.77475728352864581},{"x":0.13770873443540463,"w":0.122776985168457,"h":0.016374652779362342,"c":1,"y":0.86502841609009218,"t":"the internet]."},{"x":0.139664189611208,"t":"To improve the response, this paragraph could be expanded so that the list of","c":1,"w":0.73235468546549487,"y":0.89819714595840017,"h":0.022021327508944255},{"w":0.42163121541341148,"t":"discoveries is fully aligned with the question.","x":0.13965904177519567,"h":0.020627743729921155,"y":0.91831192200359657,"c":1},{"t":"128","x":0.093203884107912902,"h":0.01308139551465759,"w":0.036893202463785815,"c":1,"y":0.95930232546001037}]}